          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5a5dc2f35f052c8d0e8127ba1d78e4ac070bd2374a4d45986fbed128e6ca4129:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e5ab79320eb8418386a33556af34e21a",
      "statement": "spring.ai.typesafe.retry.max-retries is set to 0, disabling the TypeSafe SDK's own retry entirely, making the Resilience4j 'jev' retry instance the sole retry layer; re-enabling SDK retries would multiply requests (e.g. 429s) since both layers would retry the same failure.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/resources/application.yaml#L102-L111",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2513169e4cddd4cc5eec86f4dc44f2011f34f4fd6796a83aa0ec377d1f8fb1b3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/resources/application.yaml#L19-L20",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:786892667be78da5f6072f12207af3eb51114679dd6e888490114761a1a430bf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_382735e8ee02491c81c83c807a962a34",
      "statement": "TypeSafeConfig.jevRetryInterval is a RetryConfigCustomizer that replaces the jev retry's wait function: on a TypeSafeRateLimitException carrying retryAfterMs it waits that value clamped to [0, MAX_RETRY_AFTER_MS=10000ms]; otherwise it doubles the configured base wait-duration (1s) per attempt (1s, then 2s for 3 total attempts).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/config/TypeSafeConfig.java#L40-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f8f039576deee139f454b6a5f690f4bc421062749e3bb671c95d46eccca384d9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/config/TypeSafeConfig.java#L70-L84",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f42910f534520e680a4ce106b3c1302a8ac82ed2d7bd065552b3437377710730:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a7bbee46417d4208ac1b8d121b91977a",
      "statement": "The jev retry instance's retry-exceptions list only TypeSafeRateLimitException (429), TypeSafeInternalServerException (5xx/overloaded), and TypeSafeApiConnectionException (connection/timeout); it never retries TypeSafeBadRequestException (400), TypeSafeUnprocessableEntityException (422), or the 401/403 exceptions, and JevNotConfiguredException is ignored so an unconfigured key never burns a retry attempt.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/resources/application.yaml#L102-L111",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2513169e4cddd4cc5eec86f4dc44f2011f34f4fd6796a83aa0ec377d1f8fb1b3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b1298781131f40bf95c37dacf468756c",
      "statement": "The jev circuit breaker is the outer Resilience4j aspect (circuit-breaker-aspect-order 1) around the jev retry (retry-aspect-order 2), so it records one outcome per logical call rather than per HTTP attempt; its instance config is COUNT_BASED sliding window 20, minimum 10 calls, 50% failure-rate threshold, slow-call threshold >15s at 50% rate, wait-duration-in-open-state 60s with automatic transition to HALF_OPEN, and 3 permitted calls in HALF_OPEN.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/resources/application.yaml#L60-L84",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:365a1df18d550df3061422104008fa7ade4a3cdabbf09962929d40826e651bda:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0ccfd21d724742efa6dedc76f92318ba",
      "statement": "401 (TypeSafeAuthenticationException) and 403 (TypeSafePermissionDeniedException) are deliberately omitted from the jev circuit breaker's ignore-exceptions list, so they count as breaker failures; a bad or revoked API key returning 401/403 on every call will open the jev breaker once the failure-rate threshold is crossed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/resources/application.yaml#L74-L92",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:acbeb3849cca380aa93398d60eeadad8a9c5d5f85c6b2c295b6f0941c92a00f3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_08012605885d42ff885c5231c3dc3c6e",
      "statement": "GlobalExceptionHandler maps JevNotConfiguredException to 503, CallNotPermittedException to 503 ('Jev unavailable'), TypeSafeBadRequestException/TypeSafeUnprocessableEntityException to 422 ('Jev rejected the request'), and any other TypeSafeException to 503 ('The Jev request failed'), always using fixed app text rather than forwarding the TypeSafe exception's own message or response body.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/controller/GlobalExceptionHandler.java#L71-L105",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:edf5da9e2c8d1bfa5d6987cddad840f1c110953af343b4a736ff921ea722b28c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f934ce83eaef4e8f8cca8ace39c504fc",
      "statement": "config/JevEventLogging subscribes to the jev Retry and CircuitBreaker event publishers obtained by name from the shared registries (the same instances the @CircuitBreaker/@Retry annotations use) and logs exactly three fixed-format lines carrying only exception simple class names and numbers, never a message, response body, or API key: a retry-attempt INFO line, a retries-exhausted WARN line, and a breaker state-transition WARN line using StateTransition.name().",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/config/JevEventLogging.java#L1-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cf8c43a0fc96ca88024aabcc0a3adb09f51009c8f2247c844866786887118cf5:"
        }
      ]
    },
